It seems like there are several different bugs here:
1) pcre_study() returning NULL is not necessarily an error.  We did fix
the handling in libselinux compile_regex() in commit
14342674191ca11c4455ff7ac9b76b05173eb575 but it appears that
sefcontext_compile and libselinux load_mmap() don't handle a NULL study
result correctly.

2) The file_contexts.local file should be validated earlier, before
copying any files to /etc/selinux.

3) If errors are possible after copying files to /etc/selinux, then we
need to unlink any of the local files as part of rolling back the
transaction.
